---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BROKER } from '../config/site';
import jordan from '../assets/jordan/jordan.jpg';

const cities = await getCollection('cities');
const projects = await getCollection('projects');
const faq = await getCollection('faq');

const STATS = [
  { n: String(cities.length), l: 'Cities covered' },
  { n: String(projects.length), l: 'Projects tracked' },
  { n: String(faq.length), l: 'Questions answered' },
  { n: '$0', l: 'Cost to buyers' },
];

const DRIVERS = [
  {
    h: 'Access, not gatekeeping',
    b: 'Register once and you see every active and upcoming low-rise release, with the builder price lists and floor plans as they come out. Not a curated handful.',
  },
  {
    h: 'On the front lines',
    b: 'I am in front of these developers and these real estate lawyers every week. That is how you know which builders hit their dates and who is flexible on amendments this quarter.',
  },
  {
    h: 'Straight answers, sourced',
    b: 'Every claim on this site about rebates, deposits or warranties cites the CRA notice or Tarion page it came from, so you can check it rather than take my word for it.',
  },
  {
    h: 'Direct access to me',
    b: 'Small caseload on purpose. You deal with me from the first enquiry through to possession, not a team you get handed to.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About Jordan Buttarazzi, Broker"
  description="Jordan Buttarazzi, Broker at Valery Real Estate Inc. Helping GTA buyers navigate pre-construction low-rise with straight answers, project access and relationships with the developers and lawyers on the front lines."
  width="narrow"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'About', href: '/about' }]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-4 pt-12 sm:px-6">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-[2.3rem] leading-[1.05] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] sm:text-[3rem]">
      I wasn't a fan of pre-con.<br />
      <span class="text-accent">Then the numbers changed.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-[56ch] text-[17px] leading-[1.7] text-ink/80">
      For years the premium over resale did not make sense to me. Today some projects price at or
      even below resale, two new rebate programs are in play, and almost nothing written online has
      caught up.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- STATS -->
  <div class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-[820px] px-4 sm:px-6">
    <ul class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-px border border-rule bg-rule sm:grid-cols-4">
      {
        STATS.map((s) => (
          <li class="bg-paper-pure px-4 py-5 text-center">
            <p class="figure text-[1.75rem] leading-none text-ink">{s.n}</p>
            <p class="section-label mt-2">{s.l}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- BIO -->
  <div class="mx-auto mt-14 max-w-[820px] px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-12 sm:gap-x-10">
      <div class="sm:col-span-5">
        <figure class="tick-corners overflow-hidden border border-rule">
          <Image
            src={jordan}
            alt={`${BROKER.name}, ${BROKER.title} at ${BROKER.brokerage}`}
            widths={[340, 680, 1020]}
            sizes="(min-width: 640px) 320px, 100vw"
            loading="eager"
            class="block h-auto w-full"
          />
        </figure>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-[13px] text-ink/75">
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.5em] h-px w-2.5 shrink-0 bg-honey"></span>
            <span><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">{BROKER.name}</strong></span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.5em] h-px w-2.5 shrink-0 bg-honey"></span>
            <span>RECO Lic. <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">{BROKER.reco}</strong></span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.5em] h-px w-2.5 shrink-0 bg-honey"></span>
            <span>{BROKER.brokerage}</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.5em] h-px w-2.5 shrink-0 bg-honey"></span>
            <span>Service area: <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">GTA</strong></span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-2.5">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[0.5em] h-px w-2.5 shrink-0 bg-honey"></span>
            <span>Focus: <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">freehold low-rise</strong></span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="sm:col-span-7">
        <p class="text-[22px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em]">{BROKER.name}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-[14px] text-ink/60">
          {BROKER.title} · Pre-construction specialist · GTA
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85">
          <p>
            For a long stretch I steered people away from pre-construction. The premium over resale
            was real, the closings were years out, and you were essentially paying for the privilege
            of waiting. <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">The math did not work.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            That has genuinely changed. Some low-rise releases are now priced at or even below
            comparable resale, and two rebate programs landed this year that can return a six-figure
            amount to a qualifying buyer. For the first time in a while, the numbers are worth a
            serious look.
          </p>
          <p>
            What has not changed is the quality of the information. There is more noise and more
            misconception around pre-construction right now than I have ever seen. Rules shifted
            mid-year. Half of what is written online is out of date, and a good deal of the rest was
            written to move units.
          </p>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="mt-7 border-l-2 border-honey pl-5">
          <p class="text-[18px] leading-[1.6] font-medium text-ink">
            Their job is to sell the project. Mine is to help you decide whether it is right for
            you.
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="mt-7 space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85">
          <p>
            Which is why relationships matter more than listings. I am in front of these developers
            and these real estate lawyers every week, day in and day out. That is how you find out
            which builders actually hit their closing dates, who will move on an amendment this
            quarter, and which releases are worth your weekends.
          </p>
          <p>
            I work in freehold low-rise, detached homes, townhomes and semis, because it is where I
            can be genuinely useful. It is also the corner of the market that gets written about
            least, since most pre-construction coverage is aimed at condominiums.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MID CTA -->
  <div class="mx-auto mt-14 max-w-[820px] px-4 text-center sm:px-6">
    <a href="/vip" class="btn w-full px-6 text-sm sm:w-auto">Work with Jordan</a>
    <p class="mt-2.5 text-[12px] text-ink/55">
      Register in a minute, or <a href="/book" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">book a call</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- WHAT DRIVES THIS SERVICE -->
  <section class="mt-16 border-t border-rule bg-paper-pure/50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
      <p class="section-label">What drives this service</p>
      <ul class="mt-7 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {
          DRIVERS.map((d) => (
            <li>
              <h2 class="text-[17px] font-semibold">{d.h}</h2>
              <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/75">{d.b}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT I'M NOT -->
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What I'm not</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[16px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/85">
      A lawyer, an accountant or a mortgage agent. The rebate content on this site explains
      published CRA and Tarion rules and cites its sources. When a question turns on the law or on
      your tax position, I will tell you to take it to the right person. On a rebate worth up to
      $80,000, that is the only responsible answer.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] text-ink/55">
      Full terms are on the
      <a href="/disclaimer" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2">disclaimer page</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 border-t border-rule pt-8">
      <a href="/vip" class="btn px-6 text-sm">Register for access</a>
      <a href="/book" class="btn-secondary px-6 text-sm">Book a call</a>
      <a href={BROKER.phoneHref} class="figure text-sm text-accent underline underline-offset-2">
        {BROKER.phone}
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
